<!--
====================================================================================
_egrants_showDocsDownload.cshtml
====================================================================================

MIGRATION CHANGES SUMMARY (.NET Framework 4.8 to .NET 8):
----------------------------------------------------------
This Razor partial view handles the document download grid display and user interaction
for the Audit File Download feature.

PERFORMANCE-RELATED CHANGES:
----------------------------
1. AJAX POST REQUEST FORMAT:
   WHY CHANGED: ASP.NET Core's [FromForm] attribute expects form-encoded data, not JSON.
   
   ORIGINAL (.NET Framework):
   $.ajax({
       contentType: 'application/json; charset=utf-8',
     data: JSON.stringify(dataToSend),
url: "/Egrants/IsDownloadForm?" + urlParams
   });
   
   .NET 8:
   $.ajax({
       contentType: 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8',
       data: $.param(dataToSend, true),
       url: "/Egrants/IsDownloadForm"
});

   RATIONALE: 
   - POST with form encoding is more reliable for large payloads
   - Avoids URL length limitations (typically 2048 characters)
   - ASP.NET Core model binding works better with form data for arrays

2. URL PARAMETER HANDLING:
   WHY CHANGED: Moving data to POST body instead of query string prevents failures
   when downloading many documents (URL length exceeded errors).

3. SESSION-BASED FILE RETRIEVAL:
   WHY CHANGED: ASP.NET Core TempData has size limitations due to cookie-based storage.
   Session storage handles large byte arrays (zip files) more reliably.
   
   Download action now retrieves zip files from HttpContext.Session instead of TempData.

4. TIMEOUT CONFIGURATION:
   Set timeout: 600000 (10 minutes) to accommodate large batch downloads.
   The server-side parallel processing is faster, but network transfer may still take time.

5. ICON/STATUS DISPLAY:
   WHY CHANGED: Font Awesome's SVG replacement (data-auto-replace-svg) doesn't work 
   reliably in .NET 8 Razor views. Changed to static GIF images for consistent display:
   - new-fa-spin.gif: Download in progress
   - new-fa-circle-check.gif: Download successful
   - new-fa-circle-exclamation.gif: Download failed

CLIENT-SIDE BEHAVIOR (UNCHANGED):
---------------------------------
- DataTables grid displays documents with sorting/filtering
- Checkbox selection for batch download
- Parent/child row expansion for Financial Reports and Closeout Notifications
- Status icon updates during download process

NOTE ON SERVER-SIDE OPTIMIZATIONS:
----------------------------------
The performance improvements are primarily in DocumentService.cs (server-side):
- Parallel batch processing of downloads
- Cached HttpClient instances
- Optimized connection pooling
- Certificate caching

This view sends the same request format but benefits from faster server processing.
====================================================================================
-->
